"""Approximate a spelling-level pi/p response, not a general phonetic model.

Most tokens receive nearly zero. Greek pi, Cyrillic п, Chinese pi syllables,
and short Latin pi/pe or repeated-p fragments receive negative values.
Pu-like syllables are weaker. A p near the previous token's end adds a
negative continuation response, especially for short vowels and another p;
length, script and spacing modulate it. Short uppercase p clusters get an
extra negative response. Bare p/P/П are much stronger at a document start. State remembers only the preceding token, and resets between
documents. Completed byte-split Unicode characters are repaired when needed.
"""
